{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on the complete three-subject R3 design candidate at exact 49e6321eaae56c3f23b884c9bd2a0cd5194bdbdc, direct parent adopted 8b8f946d2b7e2e060f7a34ce76960eeee709448d. Normal evidence-only preparation binds this delivery to current request 1026ed6a. This review supplies no source closure, merge authority or contract adoption.\n\nP2: bounded license refusals cannot reliably settle the reserved lane. Main 2450 reserves one receiver-pin entry for each remaining numbered license request; 1721–1726 bounds the sequence to three and a refusal ends it. Main 1673–1676 records export-not-authorized, target-not-held or target-fixed without changing the pin. R1 candidate f52573e7 at 5199–5205 requires an explicit R3 declaration that such a refused capability request consumes its corresponding reserved entry; otherwise it is new work. R3 does not supply that declaration. Witness: license 1 applies and creates the standing pin; its ten-second window lapses, license 2 is requested after the receiving hold ends, and the licensing scope has no free new-work capacity. Its target-not-held refusal cannot draw reserve. Retrying transport then leaves the receiver without the decision needed to finalize withheld and send export-settled; the pin remains. Declare that the first authenticated decision for each bounded numbered license consumes that request's own reservation, including a refusal; duplicate decisions consume no further reserve. Preserve exact task/export/number/source binding. This is a finite existing lane, not a general capacity privilege. G3's unbounded retry/receipt capacity and G12's missing platform definitions do not disposition this specific already-reserved decision.\n\nP2: the deciding-fact prose contradicts legal late answers. Main 3502–3503 includes timed-out jobs and their deadline entry as deciding; 3505–3506 says later answers on an already decided job are history only and never become its deciding entry. Main 1130–1144 and new 1231, consistent with adopted R2 1229–1243, allow the first authentic answer on an unsuperseded timed-out job to decide passed, failed or errored. Under the new wording a late passing job retains its deadline FactRef. Destination validation at 3731 requires a check entry whose own effects set that job passed, so the legal late pass cannot support reservation. Enumerate passed/failed/errored/superseded as history-only, and explicitly make the first unsuperseded late answer replace the deciding fact. Static acceptance witness: deadline, then authentic late pass, then a statement naming that late check, then destination acceptance; a subsequent duplicate leaves the deciding fact unchanged. R1 companion N21 at 191 has related broad wording, but its actual effect rows 389–390 correctly update decidedBy from requested or timed-out. Clarify the prose rather than breaking those rows.\n\nNonblocking capacity witness correction: publication count seven at 2511–2523 is correctly fourteen publication entries. The global Used/Reserved/Free table at 2525–2536 must also account for R1's reserved closing checkpoint at 4964 and 5054–5088, or explicitly state it is a partial publication-only calculation. With otherwise unchanged Used, reserve the extra scope entry and reduce Free by one. No displayed admission outcome changes: the 25-entry request still does not fit.\n\nArchitecture: the complete request retains one history and local judgment, publication/check/declaration forms, authority, provider, workspace, device and browser contracts, all sibling asks and the actual I1 disposition obligations. O1–O10 and G1–G14 are named work, not implemented guards. Draft interface forms do not become adopted contracts through this review. The candidate was authored against R1 ba556e96; reconcile it with current R1 f52573e7 and all 139 current I1 choices, including 115–139, before claiming completed dependent delivery. H1–H6 remain explicit operator/provider/clock and evidence obligations rather than finite guarantees.\n\nSecurity: device A disappearing does not cancel an active device B hold; revocation is not instant hold termination. Renewal windows and the hosted writer fence preserve uncertainty about pushes and token effects. Person-runtime form G9 remains owed. Secret invitation parsing must isolate valid invitations, and M6 member prose is not O4 authority evidence. The landed five-fix source batch does not certify the whole M6, cancellation or credential-authority contract. U4 collections, U6 delegation and U15 cross-lane private data remain later owned scope; they are not new first-Jam prerequisites.\n\nSimplification: repair these conflicts within the existing bounded request lane and job deciding-fact rule. Existing owners retain unbounded attempts and resource limits, known-token expiry, job dispatch, fetched-copy accounting, snapshot bounds, definition activation and name trust, multireason declarations, cached revocation observations, notice fanout, platform definitions, incident records and window equality. No new gate or parallel mechanism is needed.\n\nCoverage: two assigned reviewers freshly read all main 4495 lines, corrections 495 lines and facts 723 lines, with complete changed-byte coverage against the direct parent; one also read the full two-path unified-zero diff, 1660 lines. Root inspected the full three exact-head artifact statements and current request, personally read the entire hold capacity sections 5.7–5.8 and exact license-refusal, late-job, reservation and owned-gap clauses, and relevant R1/R2 boundaries. Root does not claim personally reading the complete 195334-character combined diff. Main 397469 B SHA256 dee80ee9637cb8e43a57a04bec47da339ae32c3e467abba97aea4a23a0a13683; corrections 67956 B SHA256 2ed5f6b850c18eabd7844c90db52557fc9927676a43a53bf42148aa5ea83f94a; facts 84111 B SHA256 12db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0. Static design review only. Producer execution evidence remains attributed; no measured tenfold cost improvement, whole application acceptance, removal closure, execution, source edits or external effects are certified.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b9d5f47dc257898b2c374b4397ee7253c50ece52","binding":"evidence-only","head":"49e6321eaae56c3f23b884c9bd2a0cd5194bdbdc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a70e5a3a6fb2cf966f7884a0f2eb84f3c25f327\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:234b2af6e96ce9f64853c55626c5fcbbc8c5da85","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}